{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "moves.onroad.model",
    "description": "THE ONROAD DOMAIN MODEL. One model, no `data_sources`, and the shape that sizes it. TWO catalogues mount it -- `spikes/7c/tirewear_mount.esm`, which supplies one run's execution-database snapshot, and `../moves-onroad.esm`, which supplies the national default database -- and one thin document per RunSpec mounts THOSE and supplies the selections.\n\nIT WAS `spikes/7c/tirewear_logic.esm` UNTIL 2026-09-17, the logic half of `fixtures/process-tirewear.esm` split out at PLAN.md step 7c. It is not a tire-wear document and it is not a spike: PLAN.md step 7d asks it for a second RunSpec, `runspecs/expand-day.esm`, whose pollutant-process set it has to DISCARD two thirds of, and the name and the location moved with the role. The input source keys moved with it too -- `tw_link` is `db_link` now, because the 40 tables are the database's and not tire wear's.\n\nIT WAS THE FIXTURE'S OWN TEXT UNTIL 2026-09-17, unaltered but for the six `expression_template_imports` paths, which gained one `../` because this file sits one directory deeper than `fixtures/`. 7c' changed three things, and each is a selection the snapshot had been making for it (docs/esm-conventions.md §59):\n\n  * THE LINK. `run_linkID`, `run_countyID`, `run_zoneID` and `run_linkRoadTypeID` summed `link`, which is reading it while the execution copy has one row and is nonsense against a national `Link` of 22,610. They join on the runspec's county and road type now, and `rsc_countyID` is the one runspec selection this document did not carry.\n  * THE PHYSICS TABLE. `phys_*` read `sourceUseTypePhysicsMapping`, which MOVES synthesises from `sourceUseTypePhysics` by renaming one column and adding two this document never reads. It reads the real table, which both databases ship.\n  * THE EV SHARE. `coh_evFraction` and `coh_hasEvFraction` read `evSalesFraction`, which the default database does not ship because MOVES computes it at execution time from four tables already ingested here. `svp_salesWeight`, `coh_salesAllFuels`, `coh_salesElectric` and `coh_hasElectricRow` compute it, reproducing the snapshot's 115 rows exactly.\n\nSo the equations are no longer byte-identical to the inlined fixture's; the NUMBERS are, and run-tests.sh compares them on every run. The tolerances and the eleven `tests` blocks are unchanged.\n\nWHAT IS HERE. The logic, and the SHAPE it runs on: 57 metaparameters, the 60 `index_sets` those metaparameters size, and the 7 enums. This is `leaf-owns-shape`, and it is the only arrangement measured to load under both the Rust and the Python bindings.\n\nWHAT IS NOT HERE. `data_sources`, which `tirewear_mount.esm` supplies. That half is a choice rather than a constraint — a mounted child's `data_sources` DO merge up (docs/esm-conventions.md §49) — and it is the Phase 7 division of labour: the fixture names the tables, the component names the columns.\n\nWHY IT DOES NOT LOAD ALONE, and that is the control. It names 53 data sources it does not declare, so `esm validate` on it reports `Parameter update names data source 'db_agecategory', which the document does not declare` and more like it. run-tests.sh's 7c stage asserts that refusal: a logic half that supplied its own data would make the mount prove nothing.\n\nIT WAS SHAPE-OPEN UNTIL 2026-09-12, AND THAT SPELLING IS NOW REFUSED. As first written this file declared `index_sets` sized by metaparameter NAMES and declared no `metaparameters`, so it failed alone with `[metaparameter_unbound] document: index_sets.runspecyear_rows.size references unbound name(s) n_runspecyear` and `spikes/7c/tirewear_mount.esm` restated all 53 axes to close it. EarthSciAST PR #298 resolves a mounted leaf in its own scope and refuses the whole assembly in that form; Python had refused it all along. So the metaparameters moved here and the mount's 250-line restatement was deleted — the largest single thing this project has recovered from an upstream fix. Findings F46, F48 and F49 retired with it.\n\nTwo notes the old spelling left behind, both now explained and both since overtaken. The refusal message differed from `spikes/7a/age_group_census.esm`'s for what looked like the same defect, and four probes failed to account for it; the answer was F51 — at `9dd36c7f6` the strict close fired only when the leaf carried `expression_template_imports`, which this file does and 7a's child did not. EarthSciAST PR #317 made a mounted leaf defer an axis it cannot close instead, so that asymmetry is gone from the Rust binding. And the metaparameters below used to be declared AGAIN in the mount, because the mount's `data_sources` bind those names in `extent` and the loader API closed discovered extents only at the root (finding F50). #317 binds them where they are declared; the mount's 247-line copy was deleted and F50 retired. They are declared once, here.\n\nTHE ELEVEN `tests` BLOCKS DO NOT RUN in this assembly (F47) and are kept for the same reason 7a keeps its four: the day a mounted component's inline tests run, they are already written. The inlined fixture is still in the tree and still runs them under the fixture stage, so nothing is lost meanwhile.",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"
    ],
    "tags": [
      "moves",
      "onroad",
      "spike",
      "phase7",
      "component",
      "tirewear"
    ]
  },
  "metaparameters": {
    "n_runspecyear": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 0,
      "description": "Rows in runspecyear. Runtime-discovered by the source's own `extent`, as every entry here is: a fixture that wrote the count would be asserting the snapshot's shape rather than measuring it, and a 0 that survives to evaluation is a build error rather than a small answer (docs/esm-conventions.md §11)."
    },
    "n_runspecmonth": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 0,
      "description": "Rows in runspecmonth."
    },
    "n_runspechour": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 0,
      "description": "Rows in runspechour."
    },
    "n_runspecday": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 0,
      "description": "Rows in runspecday. The SECOND factor of the activity axis and of the output axis: two day types here, and a run with one would size both relations differently with no other edit."
    },
    "n_rateday": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 0,
      "description": "Rows in the run's RATE-side time aggregation day list. It is `runspecday` itself unless the RunSpec sets `aggregateBy`, in which case MOVES pre-aggregates the rate tables over the days the RunSpec SELECTED and then overwrites `runspecday` with the single synthesized output day -- so the two stop being the same list and this one is the one the weights are scoped to."
    },
    "n_actday": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 0,
      "description": "Rows in the run's ACTIVITY-side time aggregation day list: the day types the output day's activity covers. It is `runspecday` itself unless the RunSpec sets `aggregateBy`, where the whole week is covered whatever the RunSpec selected -- which is why `noOfRealDays` comes out 7 on a run that asked for weekdays."
    },
    "n_aggregationhour": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 0,
      "description": "Rows in the run's time aggregation hour list. It is `runspechour` itself unless the RunSpec sets `aggregateBy`, where MOVES overrides the hour selection and averages over the whole day."
    },
    "n_runspecsourcetype": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 0,
      "description": "Rows in runspecsourcetype."
    },
    "n_runspecroadtype": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 0,
      "description": "Rows in runspecroadtype."
    },
    "n_runspeccounty": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 0,
      "description": "Rows in runspeccounty. Runtime-discovered by the source's own `extent`, like every entry here -- and since 7d it sizes an AXIS rather than selecting a row: the second level of the output relation, and the trailing dimension of everything that varies with the county."
    },
    "n_runspecsourcefueltype": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 0,
      "description": "Rows in runspecsourcefueltype. The second factor of the cohort candidate grid."
    },
