          "description": "avgspeedbin.opModeIDTirewear -- 401 for bin 1 up to 416 for bin 16. THIS COLUMN IS THE WHOLE OF THE TIRE-WEAR OPERATING-MODE DISTRIBUTION (avg_speed_op_mode_distribution.rs:386-420): a speed bin already carries its tire-wear mode, so `AverageSpeedOperatingModeDistributionGenerator` emits one opModeFraction = 1 row per bin and never consults a drive schedule. The column is nullable in the schema and populated in all 16 rows here; a NULL would be stored as operating mode 0 by the Java's INSERT IGNORE, which the port records as an edge case the default database does not reach.",
          "update": {
            "kind": "data",
