          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "samplevehiclepopulation_rows"
          ],
          "description": "This sample-vehicle row's contribution to its model year's age-0 sales: sourceTypePopulation x ageFraction x stmyFraction, at age 0 so the model year IS the calendar year. A row whose source type and model year have no sourcetypeyear or age-0 sourcetypeagedistribution row weighs nothing, which is the same as MOVES skipping it (BaseRateGenerator.java:315-341)."
        },
        "svp_binOrdinal": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "samplevehiclepopulation_rows"
          ],
          "description": "Which of its cohort's source bins this row is, 1 for the first the table holds and dense from there. MOVES has no such column -- a source bin is named by its packed (fuel, engine technology, regulatory class, short model-year group) id, and the rows of one cohort are whatever they are -- and a candidate GRID cannot enumerate `whatever they are`, so this is the dense slot it enumerates instead. §22's inclusive prefix count, gated to the cohort by a join rather than by an equality filter (§20.4), which also makes it O(rows in a cohort) rather than O(rows squared)."
        },
