        "era_polProcessID": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1",
          "default": 0.0,
          "shape": [
            "emissionrateadjustment_rows"
          ],
          "description": "emissionrateadjustment.polProcessID. The national table carries 9101 and 9102 alone -- running and start ENERGY -- so every other pollutant-process misses J56 and is adjusted by 1.",
          "update": {
            "kind": "data",
            "source": "db_emissionrateadjustment",
            "from": {
              "file_variable": "polProcessID"
            }
          }
        },
        "era_sourceTypeID": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1",
          "default": 0.0,
          "shape": [
            "emissionrateadjustment_rows"
          ],
          "description": "emissionrateadjustment.sourceTypeID.",
          "update": {
            "kind": "data",
            "source": "db_emissionrateadjustment",
            "from": {
              "file_variable": "sourceTypeID"
            }
          }
        },
        "era_regClassID": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1",
          "default": 0.0,
          "shape": [
            "emissionrateadjustment_rows"
          ],
          "description": "emissionrateadjustment.regClassID. It is the key that makes this a rate-row lookup and not a cohort one: source type 51's electricity lives in regulatory class 47 and carries 0.276035, where the same source type's regulatory classes 42 and 46 carry 0.288840.",
          "update": {
            "kind": "data",
            "source": "db_emissionrateadjustment",
            "from": {
              "file_variable": "regClassID"
            }
          }
        },
        "era_fuelTypeID": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1",
          "default": 0.0,
          "shape": [
            "emissionrateadjustment_rows"
          ],
          "description": "emissionrateadjustment.fuelTypeID.",
          "update": {
            "kind": "data",
            "source": "db_emissionrateadjustment",
            "from": {
              "file_variable": "fuelTypeID"
            }
          }
        },
        "era_beginModelYearID": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1",
          "default": 0.0,
          "shape": [
            "emissionrateadjustment_rows"
          ],
          "description": "emissionrateadjustment.beginModelYearID: the lower end of J56's range predicate. The ranges are DISJOINT within a key across all 1131 rows, so the sum_product semiring below reads one row or none.",
          "update": {
            "kind": "data",
            "source": "db_emissionrateadjustment",
            "from": {
              "file_variable": "beginModelYearID"
            }
          }
        },
        "era_endModelYearID": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1",
          "default": 0.0,
          "shape": [
            "emissionrateadjustment_rows"
          ],
          "description": "emissionrateadjustment.endModelYearID.",
          "update": {
            "kind": "data",
            "source": "db_emissionrateadjustment",
            "from": {
              "file_variable": "endModelYearID"
            }
          }
        },
        "era_emissionRateAdjustment": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1",
          "default": 0.0,
          "shape": [
            "emissionrateadjustment_rows"
          ],
          "description": "emissionrateadjustment.emissionRateAdjustment: the factor `adjust.rs:586-603` multiplies the rate by, after the temperature and A/C steps and before the EV efficiency divisor. 1 in all but 26 of the rows that reach a model year this corpus runs, and those 26 are heavy-duty ELECTRIC running energy.",
          "update": {
            "kind": "data",
            "source": "db_emissionrateadjustment",
            "from": {
              "file_variable": "emissionRateAdjustment"
            }
          }
        },
        "rgc_regionID": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1",
          "default": 0.0,
          "shape": [
            "regioncounty_rows"
          ],
          "description": "regionCounty.regionID -- the FUEL region, the key `fuelSupply` is written against. It is not a county, a zone or a state: 23 of them cover the country, and their identifiers encode the PADD, the summer RVP cap and the ethanol waiver (`region.description`).",
          "update": {
            "kind": "data",
            "source": "db_regioncounty",
            "from": {
              "file_variable": "regionID"
            }
          }
        },
        "rgc_countyID": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1",
          "default": 0.0,
          "shape": [
            "regioncounty_rows"
          ],
          "description": "regionCounty.countyID. Joined to `rsc_countyID`, which is the only reason this 407,233-row table is read at all.",
          "update": {
            "kind": "data",
            "source": "db_regioncounty",
            "from": {
              "file_variable": "countyID"
            }
          }
        },
        "rgc_regionCodeID": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1",
          "default": 0.0,
          "shape": [
            "regioncounty_rows"
          ],
          "description": "regionCounty.regionCodeID: 1 is the ONROAD refinery fuel supply and 2 the NONROAD one. Every county carries both, so the gather filters rather than sums -- without the filter a county would be assigned the sum of its two region identifiers, which is a region that does not exist.",
          "update": {
            "kind": "data",
            "source": "db_regioncounty",
            "from": {
              "file_variable": "regionCodeID"
            }
          }
        },
        "rgc_fuelYearID": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1",
          "default": 0.0,
          "shape": [
            "regioncounty_rows"
          ],
          "description": "regionCounty.fuelYearID. The region a county belongs to CHANGES with the fuel year, so this is a key and not a filler; `run_fuelYearID` supplies the other side.",
          "update": {
            "kind": "data",
            "source": "db_regioncounty",
            "from": {
              "file_variable": "fuelYearID"
            }
          }
        },
        "fs_fuelRegionID": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1",
          "default": 0.0,
          "shape": [
            "fuelsupply_rows"
          ],
          "description": "fuelSupply.fuelRegionID.",
          "update": {
            "kind": "data",
            "source": "db_fuelsupply",
            "from": {
              "file_variable": "fuelRegionID"
            }
          }
        },
        "fs_fuelYearID": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1",
          "default": 0.0,
          "shape": [
            "fuelsupply_rows"
          ],
          "description": "fuelSupply.fuelYearID.",
          "update": {
            "kind": "data",
            "source": "db_fuelsupply",
            "from": {
              "file_variable": "fuelYearID"
            }
          }
        },
        "fs_monthGroupID": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1",
          "default": 0.0,
          "shape": [
            "fuelsupply_rows"
          ],
          "description": "fuelSupply.monthGroupID. The fuel supply is SEASONAL: the same region carries different formulations in January and August, which is why the criteria ratio is per county-MONTH and not per county.",
          "update": {
            "kind": "data",
            "source": "db_fuelsupply",
            "from": {
              "file_variable": "monthGroupID"
            }
          }
        },
        "fs_fuelFormulationID": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1",
          "default": 0.0,
          "shape": [
            "fuelsupply_rows"
          ],
          "description": "fuelSupply.fuelFormulationID.",
          "update": {
            "kind": "data",
            "source": "db_fuelsupply",
            "from": {
              "file_variable": "fuelFormulationID"
            }
          }
        },
        "fs_marketShare": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1",
          "default": 0.0,
          "shape": [
            "fuelsupply_rows"
          ],
          "description": "fuelSupply.marketShare, the fraction of the fuel type's volume this formulation is. It is 1.0 in every row this corpus selects -- one formulation per fuel type per region-month -- so the corpus cannot distinguish weighting the RATIOS from weighting the RATES (conventions §23). They are the same number either way: `aggregate.rs:38` accumulates `mean_base_rate * market_share` and the criteria ratio multiplies the rate, so the share factors out of the product.",
          "update": {
            "kind": "data",
            "source": "db_fuelsupply",
            "from": {
              "file_variable": "marketShare"
            }
          }
        },
        "ff_fuelFormulationID": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1",
          "default": 0.0,
          "shape": [
            "fuelformulation_rows"
          ],
          "description": "fuelFormulation.fuelFormulationID.",
          "update": {
            "kind": "data",
            "source": "db_fuelformulation",
            "from": {
              "file_variable": "fuelFormulationID"
            }
          }
        },
        "ff_fuelSubtypeID": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1",
          "default": 0.0,
          "shape": [
            "fuelformulation_rows"
          ],
          "description": "fuelFormulation.fuelSubtypeID. Two things are read off it: the fuel TYPE, through `FuelSubtype`, and whether the formulation is HIGH-ETHANOL, which is subtype 51 (E85) or 52 (E70) and not the whole of fuel type 5 -- subtype 50, plain ethanol, is fuel type 5 and is not substituted. No formulation in this database is subtype 50, so the two readings agree here and would not elsewhere (conventions §23).",
          "update": {
            "kind": "data",
            "source": "db_fuelformulation",
            "from": {
              "file_variable": "fuelSubtypeID"
            }
          }
        },
        "ff_RVP": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1",
          "default": 0.0,
          "shape": [
            "fuelformulation_rows"
          ],
          "description": "fuelFormulation.RVP, Reid vapour pressure. The ONE combustion property the high-ethanol substitution leaves alone: formulation 27002 keeps its own 7.7 while every other property becomes the E10 row's. The e10 row's RVP goes to `altRVP`, which only `altCriteriaRatio` reads and this document does not.",
          "update": {
            "kind": "data",
            "source": "db_fuelformulation",
            "from": {
              "file_variable": "RVP"
            }
          }
        },
        "ff_sulfurLevel": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "ppm",
          "default": 0.0,
          "shape": [
            "fuelformulation_rows"
          ],
          "description": "fuelFormulation.sulfurLevel, ppm. The switch between the two arms of `sulfur_switch_ratio` and the argument of its high arm. Two of the 2,158 rows are 0, whose `log` is minus infinity; every sulfur power carried here is strictly positive, so `exp(p*log(0))` is 0 and the unselected high arm stays finite.",
          "update": {
            "kind": "data",
            "source": "db_fuelformulation",
            "from": {
              "file_variable": "sulfurLevel"
            }
          }
        },
        "ff_ETOHVolume": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1",
          "default": 0.0,
          "shape": [
            "fuelformulation_rows"
          ],
          "description": "fuelFormulation.ETOHVolume, volume percent ethanol. Clamped at 10 by the E85 rows and uncapped by the gasoline ones, which is the only difference between the two fuel types' coefficient sets.",
          "update": {
            "kind": "data",
            "source": "db_fuelformulation",
            "from": {
              "file_variable": "ETOHVolume"
            }
          }
        },
        "ff_aromaticContent": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1",
          "default": 0.0,
          "shape": [
