        "cfr_fuelTypeID": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "criteriafuel_rows"
          ],
          "description": "generalFuelRatioExpression.fuelTypeID: 1 gasoline, 2 diesel, 5 ethanol."
        },
        "cfr_polProcessID": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "criteriafuel_rows"
          ],
          "description": "generalFuelRatioExpression.polProcessID: 101 THC, 201 CO, 301 NOx, all running exhaust."
        },
        "cfr_sourceTypeID": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "criteriafuel_rows"
          ],
          "description": "generalFuelRatioExpression.sourceTypeID. THIS IS A REAL KEY AND NOT A WILDCARD: the sulfur power is 0.168 for source types 11 and 21 and 0.125 for the other eleven, and the low-sulfur slope takes three different values across them. A relation that carried source type 21 alone would be right on six of this repository's seven RunSpecs and wrong on `expand-sourcetype`."
        },
        "cfr_minModelYearID": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "criteriafuel_rows"
          ],
          "description": "generalFuelRatioExpression.minModelYearID."
        },
        "cfr_maxModelYearID": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "criteriafuel_rows"
          ],
          "description": "generalFuelRatioExpression.maxModelYearID. The two ranges split at 2016/2017 for source types 11, 21 and 41-62 and at 2017/2018 for 31 and 32 -- Tier 3 phased in a year later for the light trucks -- which is why the boundary is data and not a constant."
        },
        "cfr_base": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "criteriafuel_rows"
          ],
          "description": "The divisor that turns the exponentiated polynomial into a RATIO: the same polynomial evaluated on the BASE fuel. Verbatim from the expression string, at the seventeen digits that round-trip it. It varies by one or two ULP across source types within a pollutant-process -- 0.00968296465631127 against 0.009682964656311278 for THC -- which is EPA's own summation noise in generating the strings, reproduced rather than smoothed. 1.0 on a biodiesel row, so that its unselected sulfur arm is finite."
        },
        "cfr_gpaFactor": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "criteriafuel_rows"
          ],
          "description": "The second divisor, applied only in the HIGH-sulfur arm: the base fuel's ratio at Geographic Phase-In Area sulfur. Two values per pollutant-process -- source types 11 and 21 take one, the other eleven the other."
        },
        "cfr_sulfurPower": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "criteriafuel_rows"
          ],
          "description": "The fractional power the sulfur level is raised to, written `exp(g*ln(s))` in the SQL and kept that way here. It is `sulfurModelCoeff.sulfurCoeff` for (process 1, the pollutant, M6emitter 1, the source type) -- 0.168, 0.236 and 0.351 at source type 21 -- which is a corroboration and not the source: the string is the authority, because the model-year group the table is also keyed by cannot be recovered from it. 1.0 rather than 0.0 on a biodiesel row: at power 0 a formulation with sulfur 0 would make `exp(0*log(0))` a NaN in the unselected arm."
        },
        "cfr_sulfurMultiplier": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "criteriafuel_rows"
          ],
          "description": "The multiplier inside the sample-sulfur step: 2.5, 2.36 and 1.47, which are `m6SulfurCoeff.sulfurLongCoeff` for THC, CO and NOx. 0.0 on a biodiesel row."
        },
        "cfr_bracketIntercept": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "criteriafuel_rows"
          ],
          "description": "The additive constant the two sulfur steps are added to: 1.0 before Tier 3 and 1.36251294 (THC) or 1.43164032 (NOx) after it, and 1.0 for CO in both ranges. It is the one number that says the 2017+ rows are a different regulation and not a different fuel."
        },
        "cfr_lowPivot": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "ppm",
          "shape": [
            "criteriafuel_rows"
          ],
          "description": "The sulfur level the LOW arm's linear credit is measured down from: 30 ppm before Tier 3 and 10 ppm after it, and only for the source types whose 2017 row moved."
        },
        "cfr_lowSlope": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1/ppm",
          "shape": [
            "criteriafuel_rows"
          ],
          "description": "The LOW arm's slope, per ppm. Zero for source type 11 on all three pollutants and for CO on 11, 21, 31 and 32 -- a motorcycle takes no low-sulfur credit at all -- which is a fact about the table and reads here as a coefficient rather than as a branch."
        },
        "cfr_isBiodiesel": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "criteriafuel_rows"
          ],
          "description": "1.0 on the 39 diesel rows, 0.0 on the 96 gasoline and ethanol ones. The form selector: diesel's criteria effect is `1 + min(ester,20)/100 * c` and has no sulfur arm at all."
        },
        "cfr_biodieselCoefficient": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "criteriafuel_rows"
          ],
          "description": "-0.705 for THC, -0.690 for CO and +0.110 for NOx, identical across all thirteen source types. 0.0 on a non-diesel row, which makes its unselected biodiesel arm exactly 1."
        },
        "cff_fuelTypeID": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "criteriaform_rows"
          ],
          "description": "The fuel type this coefficient set belongs to. Gasoline and ethanol carry the same six coefficients and differ only in the ethanol clamp; they are two rows because the table they come from has two, and 21 duplicated numbers is a smaller price than a key that does not match the source."
        },
        "cff_polProcessID": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "criteriaform_rows"
          ],
          "description": "The pollutant-process this coefficient set belongs to."
        },
        "cff_intercept": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "criteriaform_rows"
          ],
          "description": "The constant term of the exponent."
        },
        "cff_coefficientRVP": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "criteriaform_rows"
          ],
          "description": "The Reid-vapour-pressure coefficient; 0.0 for NOx, which has no RVP term."
        },
        "cff_coefficientT50": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "criteriaform_rows"
          ],
          "description": "The linear T50 coefficient; 0.0 for NOx."
        },
        "cff_coefficientT50Squared": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "criteriaform_rows"
          ],
          "description": "The T50-SQUARED coefficient -- `5.58244506624426e-05*T50*T50` in the THC string, and the only term in the running-exhaust polynomial whose power is not 1."
        },
        "cff_coefficientT90": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "criteriaform_rows"
          ],
          "description": "The T90 coefficient; 0.0 for NOx."
        },
        "cff_coefficientAromaticContent": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "criteriaform_rows"
          ],
          "description": "The aromatic-content coefficient; the only property all three pollutants share."
        },
        "cff_coefficientETOHVolume": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "criteriaform_rows"
          ],
          "description": "The ethanol-volume coefficient; 0.0 for CO, which has no ethanol term."
        },
        "cff_etohCap": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "criteriaform_rows"
          ],
          "description": "10 volume percent on the ethanol rows and 0.0 elsewhere: `least(10, ETOHVolume)`."
        },
        "cff_etohCapIsActive": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "criteriaform_rows"
          ],
          "description": "The indicator that turns the clamp on, for the same reason components/meteorology.esm's `pressure_is_present` is an indicator rather than a sentinel."
        },
        "run_fuelRegionID": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "runspeccounty_rows"
          ],
          "description": "The fuel region each RunSpec county draws its formulations from, at the run's fuel year. 270000000 for Washtenaw in 2020. `regionCodeID` 1 selects the onroad refinery supply; the nonroad row 2 is the other half of every county's pair."
        },
        "ff_fuelTypeID": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "fuelformulation_rows"
          ],
          "description": "The formulation's fuel type, through `FuelSubtype`. Formulations of subtypes 23 and 24 -- which `FuelSubtype` does not carry -- gather 0 and therefore match no criteria row; none of them is in any fuel supply this corpus selects."
        },
        "ff_isHighEthanol": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "fuelformulation_rows"
          ],
          "description": "Subtype 51 (E85) or 52 (E70): the formulations whose combustion properties `FuelEffectsGenerator.setup()` step 020 replaces wholesale. Three of the 2,158 rows."
        },
        "ffx_RVP": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "fuelformulation_rows"
          ],
          "description": "RVP with `changeFuelFormulationNulls` applied and NOTHING else: the property the high-ethanol substitution deliberately leaves at the formulation's own value."
        },
        "ffx_esterVolume": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "percent",
          "shape": [
            "fuelformulation_rows"
          ],
          "description": "Biodiesel ester volume, nulls filled. `e10FuelProperties` carries this column too and it is NULL in every row of it, so step 020's coalesce falls all the way through to the formulation's own value -- which is this, for a high-ethanol row as much as for a diesel one."
        },
        "ffx_sulfurLevel": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "ppm",
          "shape": [
            "runspeccounty_rows",
            "runspecmonth_rows",
            "fuelformulation_rows"
          ],
          "description": "Sulfur level after the high-ethanol substitution: 7.15 ppm for formulation 27002 in region 270000000 in August 2020, against the 8.0 the table ships."
        },
        "ffx_ETOHVolume": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "runspeccounty_rows",
            "runspecmonth_rows",
            "fuelformulation_rows"
          ],
          "description": "Ethanol volume after the substitution: 10, against the 74 the table ships. The E85 rows clamp it at 10 anyway, so this one is the substitution the corpus cannot see."
        },
        "ffx_aromaticContent": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "runspeccounty_rows",
            "runspecmonth_rows",
            "fuelformulation_rows"
          ],
          "description": "Aromatic content after the substitution: 23.14 against 0.0."
        },
        "ffx_T50": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "runspeccounty_rows",
            "runspecmonth_rows",
            "fuelformulation_rows"
          ],
          "description": "T50 after the substitution: 222.95 degrees against the sentinel 999. This is the substitution that matters -- the THC exponent carries `T50*T50`."
        },
        "ffx_T90": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "runspeccounty_rows",
            "runspecmonth_rows",
            "fuelformulation_rows"
          ],
          "description": "T90 after the substitution: 327.77 against the sentinel 999."
        },
        "cff_exponent": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "criteriaform_rows",
            "runspeccounty_rows",
            "runspecmonth_rows",
            "fuelformulation_rows"
          ],
          "description": "The argument of the single `exp` the sulfur form applies: the intercept plus six standardized terms, none of them centred or scaled. It is per (coefficient set, county, month, formulation) and not per criteria row, because the thirteen source types and two model-year ranges that share a (fuelType, polProcess) share this number exactly."
        },
        "cfr_ratio": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "criteriafuel_rows",
            "runspeccounty_rows",
            "runspecmonth_rows",
            "fuelformulation_rows"
          ],
          "description": "`criteriaRatio.ratio` for every (criteria row, county, month, formulation) cell -- the table MOVES writes at run time and the default database ships EMPTY. `ratioGPA` is not computed: the GPA expression string is IDENTICAL to the main one in all 270 criteria rows, so the blend `ratio + gpaFract*(ratioGPA - ratio)` is the identity whatever `county.GPAFract` is."
        },
        "cfr_suppliedRatio": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "criteriafuel_rows",
            "runspeccounty_rows",
            "runspecmonth_rows"
          ],
          "description": "The market-share-weighted ratio over the formulations the county's fuel supply actually carries for the criteria row's fuel type. This is where the 2,158-row formulation table collapses to the five formulations a run uses."
        },
        "ff_olefinContent": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1",
          "default": 0.0,
          "shape": [
            "fuelformulation_rows"
          ],
          "description": "fuelFormulation.olefinContent, volume percent. Read by the Complex Model and not by the closed form.",
          "update": {
