        "run_heatIndex": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "degF",
          "shape": [
            "runspeccounty_rows",
            "runspecmonth_rows"
          ],
          "description": "The heat index at the run's hour, PER COUNTY, and the number both of this chain's clamps turn on. In `process-tirewear` and `expand-day` there is one and it is 59.500000000000 degF -- hour 7, where the temperature is 59.5 and the sub-78 arm of MG-3 returns it unchanged. In `expand-counties` there are three and they differ, which is the point. It is now COMPUTED by `zmh_heatIndex` rather than read off `ZoneMonthHour.heatIndex`, and because that arm is an identity the computed value is the ingested one bit for bit.\n\nTHE TWO MARGINS, both measured against this snapshot's own `monthgrouphour` row (A -3.63154, B 0.072465, C -0.000276): the A/C activity quadratic crosses 0 at a heat index of 67.4340633418 degF, so 59.5 is 7.934 degF below the clamp; the EV suppression fires above 67.0 degF, so 59.5 is 7.500 degF below it. The prose here used to say 66.900001525879 with margins of 0.3 and 0.1 degF. That is `mixed-onroad`'s hour 9, not this fixture's hour 7 -- a claim copied across documents, contradicted by this file's own `the_run_scope` assertion of 59.5 and by docs/process-tirewear.md 7.3's \"59.5 is 7.5 degF below\". docs/meteorology-generator.md 8.2 carries the margin table for all eight retargeted fixtures."
        },
        "run_acActivityTermA": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "runspeccounty_rows",
            "runspecmonth_rows"
          ],
          "description": "S15(d)'s constant term, read from monthgrouphour. Constant across the run's counties, and shaped over them anyway: it is ADDED to a per-county heat index, and broadcasting it here is cheaper to read than an aggregate at every use."
        },
        "run_acActivityTermB": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1/degF",
          "shape": [
            "runspeccounty_rows",
            "runspecmonth_rows"
          ],
          "description": "S15(d)'s linear term. Constant across the run's counties, and shaped over them anyway: it is ADDED to a per-county heat index, and broadcasting it here is cheaper to read than an aggregate at every use."
        },
        "run_acActivityTermC": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1/degF^2",
          "shape": [
            "runspeccounty_rows",
            "runspecmonth_rows"
          ],
          "description": "S15(d)'s quadratic term. Constant across the run's counties, and shaped over them anyway: it is ADDED to a per-county heat index, and broadcasting it here is cheaper to read than an aggregate at every use."
        },
        "run_acActivityRaw": {
          "type": "unknown",
