          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "sourcebin_rows",
            "runspeccounty_rows"
          ],
          "description": "S12, source_bin_distribution_generator.rs:1590-1637: the same activity re-attributed to the fuel each cohort actually BURNS. The equipped and used sides must agree on model year, engine technology, regulatory class and model-year group and differ only in the fuel. This is the column the base rate is weighted by (sbweighted.rs:148-165), and using the equipped one instead is a factor of 55 on the E85 rows. PER COUNTY, because `fuelUsageFraction` is keyed by county -- E85 is not available everywhere, so the same cohort grid is re-attributed differently in each. The self-join matches on the SOURCE TYPE as well as the model year, engine technology and regulatory class: with one source type selected that was implied, and with two a passenger car would be re-attributed a light commercial truck's activity."
