          "description": "Does this rate row put a number in `MOVESOutput`? Not the same question as `rt_survives`: a CHAINED pollutant-process -- PM2.5 tire wear, computed from PM10 by a ratio -- has `rt_isSelected` 0 on every one of its rows, because it has no `pollutantprocessmodelyear` row at all, and is emitted anyway. This is the predicate the two emission counts read; `rt_survives` stays what it was, the rate selection. The chain arm asks whether the ratio EXISTS, not whether it is positive: `CrankcaseEmissionRatio` carries crankcaseRatio = 0 for diesel model years 2001 and later, and MOVES emits those 19 cohorts as zeros. Testing `rt_chainRatio > 0` instead drops them, which is the same mistake as reading an unrated cohort off a rate of zero (conventions §69)."
        },
