        },
        {
          "_comment": "MG-1's last leg: the ambient pressure the two humidity measures divide by, gathered onto the county axis. MOVES reaches it as ZoneMonthHour -> Zone -> County and this chain as runspeccounty -> County, which is the same key.",
          "lhs": "run_barometricPressure",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "faq",
            "args": [],
            "semiring": "sum_product",
            "output_idx": [
              "g"
            ],
            "ranges": {
              "g": {
                "from": "runspeccounty_rows"
              },
              "y": {
                "from": "county_rows"
              }
            },
            "join": [
              {
                "on": [
                  [
                    "rsc_countyID",
                    "cty_countyID"
                  ]
                ]
              }
            ],
            "expr": {
              "op": "index",
              "args": [
                "cty_barometricPressure",
                "y"
              ]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "_comment": "MG-6. The fixtures read `ZoneMonthHour.vaporPartialPressure`; this chain has no execution database and computes it from the temperature and relative humidity it already computes -- the same two columns the heat index reads, so the three meteorological derivatives cannot disagree about which hour they are for.",
          "lhs": "run_vaporPartialPressure",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "apply_expression_template",
            "args": [],
            "name": "vapor_partial_pressure_from_weather",
            "bindings": {
              "temperature_degF": "run_temperature",
              "rel_humidity_percent": "run_relHumidity"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "_comment": "MG-7, specific humidity: g water per kg DRY air. The denominator subtracts the vapour pressure from the ambient pressure because the air it measures against is dry; the mole fraction's does not, and that one term is the only difference between the two.",
          "lhs": "run_specificHumidity",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "apply_expression_template",
            "args": [],
            "name": "specific_humidity",
            "bindings": {
              "vapor_pressure_kpa": "run_vaporPartialPressure",
              "barometric_pressure_inhg": "run_barometricPressure"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "_comment": "MG-7, water mole fraction: moles of water per mole of AMBIENT air. CFR 1065's argument.",
          "lhs": "run_molWaterFraction",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "apply_expression_template",
            "args": [],
            "name": "mol_water_fraction",
            "bindings": {
              "vapor_pressure_kpa": "run_vaporPartialPressure",
              "barometric_pressure_inhg": "run_barometricPressure"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "_comment": "The two humidity equations as one-row relations, so selecting one is a `join.on` like every other key selection here rather than an `==` inside a filter (conventions 20.4).",
          "lhs": "run_humidityEqCFR86",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "makearray",
            "args": [],
            "regions": [
              [
                [
                  1,
                  1
                ]
