        {
          "_comment": "J62: `FuelEffectsGenerator.setup()` step 020, `alterHighEthanolFuelProperties`. A subtype-51 or -52 formulation takes this property from `e10FuelProperties` at its own (fuel region, fuel year, month group); every other formulation keeps its own value, nulls filled. The `run_rows` range carries no index in the expression and is NOT spare -- it is what lets `run_fuelYearID` resolve as the right side of a key pair (EarthSciML/EarthSciAST#437); drop it and the gather sums this property over all 64 fuel years. CANONICAL'S THREE-LEVEL COALESCE IS NOT PORTED: step 020 falls back from the region's row to the national row 0 and then to the formulation's own value, and this gather stops at the first. Not one of the 15,360 non-national rows has a NULL in any column read here, so the fallback has nothing to do wherever a regional row exists -- and where one does not, this contracts to 0 for EVERY formulation rather than for the high-ethanol ones alone, which moves the criteria ratio by a factor of three and is therefore loud.",
