        {
          "_comment": "The two halves of `criteriaRatio`, selected rather than summed -- for the same reason `rtMode_rate` selects between the two rate tables (conventions §67.1). They are disjoint by construction: `generalFuelRatioExpression` carries no gasoline row before model year 2001 and the Complex Model runs on nothing else, so no rate row has both. An uncovered row is scaled by 1 and not by 0, which is what `adjust.rs:483-491` does when the lookup misses -- every electricity and CNG cohort, diesel after model year 2006 and ethanol before 2001.",
