        {
          "_comment": "J59: `calculate_nox_k`'s two arms, adjust.rs:168-188. The equation name is a TEXT column, so the branch is a second key pair against a one-row relation and the two arms are separate aggregates -- which is also what keeps the CFR 86 rows' NULL `humidityTermB` out of the other arm's arithmetic. The `run_rows` range carries no index in the expression and is NOT spare: it is what lets the second key pair's right side -- `run_humidityEqCFR86`, a one-row relation over `run_rows` -- resolve to a loop symbol at all. Dropping it does not raise; the pair is silently ignored and BOTH arms fire for every fuel type (EarthSciAST #437).",
          "lhs": "rt_humidityCFR86",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "faq",
            "args": [],
            "semiring": "sum_product",
            "output_idx": [
              "b",
