      "tests": [
        {
          "id": "the_run_scope_comes_from_the_execution_database",
          "description": "Year 2020, August, hour 7, source type 21, road type 4, county 26161, zone 261610. The RunSpec XML says month 7 and hour 6; the execution database says 8 and 7, and it is the authority (docs/mixed-onroad.md 0.1). 59.5 degF is the hour's temperature and its heat index -- the two columns are equal in every row of this snapshot and the document still reads them separately, because adjust.rs uses the first for the temperature adjustment and the second for the A/C term and the EV suppression.",
          "time_span": {
            "start": 0.0,
            "end": 0.0
          },
          "assertions": [
            {
              "variable": "run_yearID",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 2020.0,
              "coords": {
                "run_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "run_monthID",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 8.0,
              "coords": {
                "run_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "run_hourID",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 7.0,
              "coords": {
                "run_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "rst_sourceTypeID",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 21.0,
              "coords": {
                "runspecsourcetype_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "run_roadTypeID",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 4.0,
              "coords": {
                "run_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "run_countyID",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 26161.0,
              "coords": {
                "run_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "run_zoneID",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 261610.0,
              "coords": {
                "run_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "run_stateID",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 26.0,
              "coords": {
                "run_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "run_baseYearIsAnalysisYear",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 1.0,
              "coords": {
                "run_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "run_fuelYearID",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 2020.0,
              "coords": {
                "run_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "run_hpmsVtypeID",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 25.0,
              "coords": {
                "runspecsourcetype_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "run_daysInMonth",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 31.0,
              "coords": {
                "run_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "run_monthGroupID",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 8.0,
              "coords": {
                "run_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "run_temperature",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 59.5,
              "coords": {
                "run_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "run_heatIndex",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 59.5,
              "coords": {
                "run_rows": 1
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "the_three_pollutant_processes_and_the_chain_between_them",
          "description": "The run's whole pollutant scope, unpacked from `runspecpollutantprocess` and `runspecchainedto` rather than written down. 9101 is Total Energy x Running Exhaust and is the only ENERGY pollutant here, so it is the only one S18 divides by 1,055,055.9; 11710 is PM2.5 Tirewear x Tirewear and carries its own emissionrate rows; 10710 is PM10 Tirewear, which carries NONE and is chained from 11710. `rspp_chainInputPolProcessID` is 11710 on the middle row and 0 on the other two, and that 0 -- the additive identity of the LEFT JOIN, which is no pollutant-process -- is what makes the chain term vanish without a branch.\n\nTHE PROCESS IDS ARE 1 AND 10 AND THAT MATTERS TWICE. It is the process, not the pollutant, that decides which generator wrote a pollutant-process's operating-mode weights (`rspp_usesAvgSpeedModes`), and it is the process digit that the SCC and the output's own processID column carry -- 2201210410 against brake wear's 2201210409, one digit apart.",
          "time_span": {
            "start": 0.0,
            "end": 0.0
          },
          "assertions": [
            {
              "variable": "rspp_pollutantID",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 91.0,
              "coords": {
                "runspecpollutantprocess_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "rspp_pollutantID",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 107.0,
              "coords": {
                "runspecpollutantprocess_rows": 2
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "rspp_pollutantID",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 117.0,
              "coords": {
                "runspecpollutantprocess_rows": 3
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "rspp_processID",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 1.0,
              "coords": {
                "runspecpollutantprocess_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "rspp_processID",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 10.0,
              "coords": {
                "runspecpollutantprocess_rows": 2
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "rspp_processID",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 10.0,
              "coords": {
                "runspecpollutantprocess_rows": 3
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "rspp_isEnergy",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 1.0,
              "coords": {
                "runspecpollutantprocess_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "rspp_isEnergy",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 0.0,
              "coords": {
                "runspecpollutantprocess_rows": 2
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "rspp_isEnergy",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 0.0,
              "coords": {
                "runspecpollutantprocess_rows": 3
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "rspp_unitDivisor",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 1055055.9,
              "coords": {
                "runspecpollutantprocess_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "rspp_unitDivisor",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 1.0,
              "coords": {
                "runspecpollutantprocess_rows": 2
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "rspp_unitDivisor",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 1.0,
              "coords": {
                "runspecpollutantprocess_rows": 3
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "rspp_chainInputPolProcessID",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 0.0,
              "coords": {
                "runspecpollutantprocess_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "rspp_chainInputPolProcessID",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 11710.0,
              "coords": {
                "runspecpollutantprocess_rows": 2
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "rspp_chainInputPolProcessID",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 0.0,
              "coords": {
                "runspecpollutantprocess_rows": 3
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "the_drive_cycle_scaffolding_is_a_single_physics_row_and_two_data_thresholds",
          "description": "The three facts W's correctness rests on that are not W itself: the braking thresholds are READ from operatingmode's Braking row rather than written as drivecycle.rs's -2.0 and -1.0 literals; the drive-cycle axis is exactly the vehicles this run drives, which here is one; and every average-speed bin's bracketing weights sum to 1, which is what catches a duplicated bracket speed or a bin with no bracket.\n\nTHE MIDDLE ONE IS THREE ASSERTIONS AND NOT ONE AS OF 7d-next. It used to be `run_physicsRowsSelected == 1` per source type, and it was the document's statement that a source type has one vehicle -- which is true of a passenger car and false of everything heavier, so it read as a fact about the model and was really a fact about the fixture. Now it is the recomputation of `n_physicsRow` (1 here, 4 at source types 21 and 32, 40 at five), plus the two ways the axis can be wrong without changing the shape of anything: a selected vehicle past the end of the axis, and a rate row whose regulatory class has no vehicle at all. Both are silent and both are LOW, which is the failure mode `run_sourceBinsDropped` was added for one relation up.",
          "time_span": {
            "start": 0.0,
            "end": 0.0
          },
          "assertions": [
            {
              "variable": "run_brakeRate1Sec",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": -2.0,
              "coords": {
                "run_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "run_brakeRate3Sec",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": -1.0,
              "coords": {
                "run_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "run_physicsRowsSelected",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 1.0,
              "coords": {
                "run_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "run_physicsRowsDropped",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 0.0,
              "coords": {
                "run_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "run_rateRowsWithoutPhysics",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 0.0,
              "coords": {
                "run_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "run_fuelUsageWildcardCount",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 5.0,
              "coords": {
                "run_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "asb_scheduleFractionTotal",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 1.0,
              "coords": {
                "avgspeedbin_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "asb_scheduleFractionTotal",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 1.0,
              "coords": {
                "avgspeedbin_rows": 8
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "asb_scheduleFractionTotal",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 1.0,
              "coords": {
                "avgspeedbin_rows": 16
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "the_cohort_row_set_is_the_same_125_for_both_rate_paths",
          "description": "125 of the 164 candidates survive `stmyFraction > 0`, and all 125 reach an emissionrate row, for BOTH computed pollutant-processes -- which is the claim that lets one cohort rank serve all three output blocks and is asserted rather than assumed. `pp_selectedBinCount` is 125, 0, 125: the middle zero is the chained pollutant, which has no pollutantprocessmodelyear rows and therefore no source-bin distribution of its own, and whose 125 output rows come from the chain instead -- `run_chainedRowCount` counts them. `run_binSelectionTotal` at 250 is the same fact summed, and would still be 250 if the two rate paths selected DIFFERENT 125s, which is why the per-pollutant-process counts are asserted beside it.\n\nTHE THREE COUNTS ARE OVER BINS AND `cohortSurvivorCount` IS OVER COHORTS, AND THIS RUN IS WHERE THE TWO COINCIDE. A passenger car's `samplevehiclepopulation` rows are one per (model year, fuel type) -- regulatory class 20 throughout, engine technology 1 or 30 but never both in one cohort -- so `n_sourceBin` is 1 here and the bin relation IS the cohort relation, row for row. `run_sourceBinsDropped` is what says the 1 is enough rather than merely unrefuted: it counts the bins a selected cohort holds beyond the last slot, and a light commercial truck would put 123 of them there.\n\nTHAT THE TWO RATE PATHS AGREE ON THE 125 IS NOT THE SAME CLAIM HERE AS IN process-brakewear, AND IT IS LESS OBVIOUS. There the two paths met different source bins because their shortModYrGroupIDs differed; here 11710's is 0 on every model year, so its 31 emissionrate source bins are distinguished by regulatory class, engine technology and fuel alone. A cohort that reached a 9101 rate and no 11710 rate would show up as a count below 125 rather than as a missing output row, because the output relation's rank is built once.",
          "time_span": {
            "start": 0.0,
            "end": 0.0
          },
          "assertions": [
            {
              "variable": "cohortSurvivorCount",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 125.0,
              "coords": {
                "run_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "run_binSelectionTotal",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 250.0,
              "coords": {
                "run_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "run_chainedRowCount",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 125.0,
              "coords": {
                "run_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "run_sourceBinsDropped",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 0.0,
              "coords": {
                "run_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
