        {
          "id": "the_activity_chain_reproduces_the_worked_examples",
          "description": "docs/process-tirewear.md 6.1 and 6.3, at the four named stages a wrong factor shows up at. The activity half is shared by all three pollutants -- tire wear is weighted by the same source-hours-operating as running-exhaust energy -- so an error here moves all 750 rows. It is also byte-identical to `process-brakewear`'s: `sho`, `avgspeeddistribution`, `driveschedulesecond`, `sourcetypeagedistribution` and `hourvmtfraction` are the same rows in both snapshots, which is why the retarget audit of docs/process-tirewear.md 6.4 reproduced 250 rows and found nothing new. travelFraction normalised over the whole HPMS group is 1.609175e-03 for the oldest cohort; over source type 21 alone it is 4.10e-03 and every row is 2.55x high. averageSpeed is the ARITHMETIC mean. The four `sho` values are the snapshot's own, to its six stored significant figures.",
