        {
          "id": "the_EV_temperature_arm_is_live_at_this_hour_and_the_AC_arm_is_not",
          "description": "The two clamps of S15, at 59.5 degF -- the same hour as `process-brakewear`, and asserted here because a shared spine that is only checked in one fixture is checked in none of them once that fixture moves. The A/C activity quadratic is -0.29698 and clamps to 0, so the A/C factor is again exactly 0.\n\nThe EV temperature arm does NOT clamp: (59.5 - 72)(0.00225 + 0.00028 x (59.5 - 72)) = +0.015625, so the factor is 1.015625 and the 84 energy/electricity rows carry it. Two things have to be right to get there and neither is visible in a run whose hour makes the arm clamp: the `temperatureadjustment` row is keyed regClassID 0, a WILDCARD, and reaching it needs the two-step precedence of lib/adjustments.esm's `exact_else_wildcard` -- `rt_hasTempAdjustExact` is asserted at 0 to pin that the exact-class lookup finds nothing, so the answer comes from the wildcard arm and not from a clamp; and the branch is gated on pollutant 91 AND process 1 together (adjust.rs:107), so a TIRE-WEAR electricity cohort takes the standard quadratic instead and its factor is exactly 1. That last assertion is the one that changes meaning here: the gate now has to reject process 10 rather than process 9.",
